<p>When you open a shop, HardPoint starts you with one branch called <strong>Main branch</strong>, Kenya's VAT rates and the usual units (piece, metre, kilogram, bag and so on). The owner's dashboard shows a <strong>Set up your shop</strong> checklist until you've been through it. It takes most shops an afternoon.</p>

<h2>1. Branches and tills</h2>
<p>In <strong>Settings → Branches</strong>, rename the main branch and add its address and phone number (they go on receipts and invoices). Add a branch for each shop or yard that keeps its own stock. Then in <strong>Settings → Tills</strong> add a till for each counter that takes money.</p>

<h2>2. Taxes</h2>
<p>Check <strong>Settings → Tax rates</strong>. VAT at 16% is the default for new products; zero-rated and exempt rates are there for the goods that need them. Prices you enter include VAT.</p>

<h2>3. Products</h2>
<p>The quickest way is to <%= link_to "import a spreadsheet", help_article_path("importing-products"), class: "link" %> of your price list. You can also add products one at a time, with barcodes, units of sale (a bag, or a metre off the roll) and reorder levels.</p>

<h2>4. Staff</h2>
<p>Invite everyone who uses HardPoint in <strong>Settings → Staff</strong> and give them a role. See <%= link_to "Staff, roles and PINs", help_article_path("staff-and-roles"), class: "link" %>.</p>

<h2>5. A test receipt</h2>
<p>Print a test receipt from the checklist to check the printer's paper width and that the text fits. See <%= link_to "Tills, receipt printers and cash drawers", help_article_path("tills-and-printers"), class: "link" %>.</p>

<h2>Optional: M-Pesa and KRA eTIMS</h2>
<p>Connect your Paybill or Till number and your branch's eTIMS control unit in <strong>Settings → Integrations</strong>. You can sell without them and add them later.</p>
